TITLE: YGGDRASIL A50 / T10B — Frozen Recovery × Challenge Push-Pull Factorial Composition
DATE: 2026-09-22
STATUS: PREREGISTERED CROSS-LAYER COMPOSITION EXPERIMENT / NON-CANONICAL
TRACK: YGGDRASIL TRAINING T10B / APPLICATION-A
BASE SUBSTRATE: A45 ECHO_PHASE
RECOVERY DONOR: A48-validated G5_FULL from F47
MACRO DONOR: A49 CH_PUSH_PULL from F49
BRANCH: dg1a-ar

WHY A50 EXISTS

A48 established that
G5_FULL is a reproducible,
safe,
moderate recovery aid.

Across five independent manifests,
D3 recovery improved in the same direction
in all five replicates.

The mechanism reduces refractory debt
and returns some cells
to recruitable U sooner.

A49 independently established that
a surviving A45 cooperative core
can strongly control
the currently recruitable U periphery
during challenge.

A49 CH_PUSH_PULL:

reduces near-core adverse recruitment;

increases near-core favored recruitment;

raises burst-end favored committed mass;

and raises the next-cycle
challenge-onset favored-core baseline.

But A49 did not cross
the frozen macro-information threshold.

The post-A49 unresolved-reservoir diagnostic
identified why the local field
has limited macro leverage.

At hard 5:3 burst end:

roughly two thirds
to three quarters
of unresolved mass
is refractory;

only roughly one tenth
to one fifth
is immediately recruitable U.

Therefore A48 and A49
operate on different measured bottlenecks.

A48:

increases availability.

A49:

organizes available U.

A50 asks whether
those independently validated layers
compose super-additively
without retuning either one.

F50 FREEZE

Let the exact A50 implementation
freeze commit be:

F50.

No real A50 world,
population outcome,
factorial interaction,
qualification result,
or scientific comparison
may be derived before F50 exists.

WORLD SHAPE

384 fresh post-F50 trials.

48 contexts x 8 replicas.

48 cells.

48 epochs.

Environmental families remain
structurally identical
to A45/A48/A49.

BASE ORGANISM

Use A45 ECHO_PHASE
exactly as the base substrate.

Preserve:

A36 ecology;

A40 signed temporal state;

A43 margin-weighted
cooperative reinforcement;

A44 local
SUPPORT / CHALLENGE / NEUTRAL mode;

A44 support-gated
active margin recruitment;

A45 one-epoch,
non-recursive cooperative echo.

No A37 lineage state exists.

RECOVERY FACTOR — FROZEN G5_FULL

The recovery factor
is the exact F47/A48 G5_FULL behavior.

No gate,
timing,
threshold,
radius,
or action changes.

For a refractory FC / FS cell i
relative to former side s:

G5(i) is true iff:

local mode relative to s
is SUPPORT;

post-update aligned
former-side margin M_post(i,s) > 0;

and

current raw same-side
cooperative field Q_raw(i,s) > 0.

Q_raw uses:

current refractory-stage
committed-neighbor topology;

weighted by beginning-of-epoch B_pre margins.

This preserves
the repaired A46 / F47 timing.

If G5 is true:

state_i := U;

timer_i := 0;

in the current epoch.

The cell receives:

no direct recommitment;

no former-side recruitment bonus;

no inherited echo.

It becomes an ordinary eligible U cell
for the later same-epoch recruitment stage.

If G5 is false:

use the A45 parent refractory timer
exactly unchanged.

MACRO FACTOR — FROZEN CH_PUSH_PULL

The macro factor
is the exact A49
challenge occupancy push-pull rule.

After:

current evidence update;

refractory processing;

H release;

committed-state A45 defection decisions;

and A45 trace update;

freeze the surviving committed core.

For each surviving committed cell,
use the existing A44
local mode.

For eligible U target i:

Q_C_ch_occ(i)

is the radius-3 mean
of surviving C cells
whose local C mode is CHALLENGE.

Q_S_ch_occ(i)

is defined analogously.

Use:

R_core = 3.

ETA = 1/2.

No new gain.

No threshold.

No distance kernel.

For C recruitment:

lambda_C'
=
(
lambda_C_parent
+
ETA * Q_C_ch_occ
)
*
(
1 - Q_S_ch_occ
).

For S:

lambda_S'
=
(
lambda_S_parent
+
ETA * Q_S_ch_occ
)
*
(
1 - Q_C_ch_occ
).

lambda_H is unchanged.

The parent lambdas
are the exact A45 recruitment intensities,
including A44 support-gated
active margin recruitment.

COMBINED-ARM TIMING

The cross-layer interaction
is intentionally causal and ordered.

Within each epoch:

1. capture B_pre;

2. update signed B;

3. process refractory FC/FS cells;

4. if recovery factor is active,
   apply frozen G5_FULL
   and release qualifying cells to U;

5. process H release;

6. execute A45 committed-state
   cooperative-echo defection decisions;

7. update the non-recursive
   A45 raw-Q trace;

8. freeze the surviving committed core;

9. compute A49 challenge occupancy fields;

10. form the eligible U set,
    including same-epoch
    G5-released cells;

11. execute ordinary U recruitment,
    with CH_PUSH_PULL
    only when the macro factor is active.

Thus G5 may increase
the number of cells
available to the A49 field
in the same epoch.

A50 adds no direct coupling
other than this pre-existing
state-flow composition.

FACTORS

Recovery factor R:

0 = parent A45 refractory behavior.

1 = frozen G5_FULL.

Macro factor P:

0 = parent A45 recruitment behavior.

1 = frozen A49 CH_PUSH_PULL.

ARMS

Exactly eight arms.

D2:

D2_R0_P0_BASE;
D2_R1_P0_G5;
D2_R0_P1_PUSH_PULL;
D2_R1_P1_COMBINED.

D3:

D3_R0_P0_BASE;
D3_R1_P0_G5;
D3_R0_P1_PUSH_PULL;
D3_R1_P1_COMBINED.

No exclusion-only arm.

No active-only arm.

A49 already measured
the single macro components.

No G5 dose sweep.

No stagger arm.

A48 already closed
the recovery-tuning loop.

COMMON-RANDOM DESIGN

Within each D family,
all four arms use
the exact same inherited
A45 ECHO_PHASE
stateless action-random identity.

G5 is deterministic
given local state.

CH_PUSH_PULL is deterministic
given local state.

Worlds,
sensor noise,
heterogeneity,
and inherited event salts
are shared.

No sequential RNG cursor exists.

Therefore the factorial comparison
isolates the two mechanism factors.

PRIMARY TARGET

Hard 5:3 contexts:

46 and 47.

Secondary non-regression:

6:2 contexts 44 and 45.

Balanced control:

40 through 43.

True reversal:

all inherited reversal families.

