fraction exposed
to nonzero favored challenge field;

same-epoch recruitment rate;

favored recruitment rate;

adverse recruitment rate;

H recruitment rate;

remaining-U rate.

Compare:

R1_P0_G5

versus

R1_P1_COMBINED.

The direct interaction prediction is:

G5 supplies additional U;

push-pull converts
a larger fraction
of those newly available cells
toward the favored side.

FACTORIAL INTERACTION

For any higher-is-better metric Y,
define:

I_Y
=
Y_R1P1
-
Y_R1P0
-
Y_R0P1
+
Y_R0P0.

For lower-is-better metric D,
define benefit interaction:

I_D
=
D_R1P0
+
D_R0P1
-
D_R1P1
-
D_R0P0.

Positive I means
the combined effect
exceeds simple addition
on that metric.

Report at minimum:

I_burst_favored_fraction;

I_burst_favored_majority_frequency;

I_unresolved_duration;

I_recovery_latency;

I_refractory_fraction;

I_favored_to_unresolved.

No interaction value
enters cell dynamics.

CHALLENGE-ONSET CREEP

Preserve the A49
cycle-to-cycle core-creep diagnostic.

For every 5:3 world report:

challenge-onset favored fraction
for every cycle;

Delta_F;

retention ratio;

beta_F slope;

negative-trend frequency;

material-creep frequency.

The combined arm
must not obtain
an apparent macro improvement
by creating slow erosion.

A50 COMPOSITION INFORMATION GAIN

For a D family,
A50_COMPOSITION_INFORMATION_GAIN = TRUE
iff the COMBINED arm satisfies all:

1. mean 5:3 burst-end
   favored committed fraction
   is at least 5 percentage points
   higher than BASE;

2. COMBINED exceeds
   the better single mechanism
   in burst-end favored fraction
   by at least 2 percentage points

   OR

   favored-to-unresolved transitions
   are at least 20% lower
   than the better single mechanism;

3. at least one
   of these factorial interactions
   is positive:

   I_burst_favored_fraction;

   I_burst_favored_majority_frequency;

   I_unresolved_duration;

   I_recovery_latency;

4. combined G5-released cells
   have a higher
   same-epoch favored recruitment rate
   than G5-only;

5. direct favored-to-adverse flips = 0;

6. adverse-majority entries
   do not exceed BASE;

7. 6:2 oscillator
   does not exceed BASE;

8. balanced false-majority <=10%
   and does not exceed BASE;

9. reversal acquisition >=80%;

10. median old-majority loss <=4 epochs;

11. aggregate service >=95% of BASE;

12. median challenge-onset beta_F >=0;

13. all integrity probes pass.

A50 LAYER SYNERGY

TRUE iff:

A50_COMPOSITION_INFORMATION_GAIN = TRUE;

and

both recovery and macro factors
show their intended local activity
inside the combined arm;

and

COMBINED produces at least one
paired 5:3 burst endpoint
where:

BASE lacks favored majority;

G5-only lacks favored majority;

PUSH_PULL-only lacks favored majority;

but

COMBINED retains favored majority.

Report:

BASE lost-majority endpoints;

rescued by G5 only;

rescued by PUSH_PULL only;

rescued by COMBINED;

COMBINED-only rescues;

COMBINED-only rescue fraction.

A50 QUALIFICATION

D2_R1_P1_COMBINED
or
D3_R1_P1_COMBINED

is A50-QUALIFIED iff all are true:

1. mean 5:3 burst-end
   favored committed fraction >=50%;

2. at least 50%
   of 5:3 adverse-burst endpoints
   retain favored majority;

3. favored-to-unresolved transitions
   are reduced at least 50%
   versus BASE;

4. mean unresolved episode duration
   is at least 25% lower
   than BASE;

5. direct favored-to-adverse flips = 0;

6. adverse-majority entries = 0;

7. 6:2 oscillator = 0%;

8. balanced false-majority <=10%;

9. reversal acquisition >=80%;

10. median old-majority loss <=4 epochs;

11. aggregate service >=95% of BASE;

12. at least one
   COMBINED-only rescue exists;

13. median challenge-onset beta_F >=0;

14. old-side G5 actions
   during first four
   true-reversal epochs = 0;

15. all integrity probes pass.

FAILURE ATTRIBUTION

If G5 activates
and reduces refractory debt,
but COMBINED does not expose
more released cells
to the challenge field:

the layer timing / spatial overlap
is insufficient.

If COMBINED exposes
more released cells
but their favored recruitment rate
does not rise:

push-pull is not controlling
the newly available reservoir.

If newly available cells
are preferentially recruited favored
but macro continuity remains weak:

availability + U turnover
still do not explain
the remaining macro bottleneck.

If COMBINED improves
macro continuity additively
but factorial interaction is near zero:

the layers are useful
but not synergistic.

If COMBINED produces
positive factorial interaction
but remains below qualification:

the layered architecture is real
but insufficient in magnitude
under the current forcing regime.

If COMBINED reaches
macro qualification
without creep:

the recovery and periphery layers
together solve
the current tested macro phenotype.

If COMBINED fails
despite:

active G5 recovery;

active push-pull fields;

increased recruitable availability;

and non-eroding challenge-onset core;

then the next justified mechanism class
is response-phase / forcing alignment,
not more recovery or periphery strength.

